<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.4: Dividing Polynomial Functions and the Remainder Theorem</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01620</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.4: Dividing Polynomial Functions and the Remainder Theorem</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9797dc54-9f7d-41f7-b250-34eeb66e11db</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Divide the polynomial functions. Find the quotient value.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(f(x)=x^2-5x-24\) 
        \(g(x)=x+3\)
        
        \((\frac{f}{g})(x) =\) ___________
        
        \(f(-3) =\) ___________
     </para>
    <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  
  <para>\((\frac{f}{g})(x)=x-8\)
\(f(-3)=0\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(f(x)=x^2-15x+54\)
        \(g(x)=x-9\)
        
        \((\frac{f}{g})(x) =\) ___________
        
        \(f(9) =\) ___________
     </para>
    <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  
  <para>\((\frac{f}{g})(x)=x-6\)
\(f(9)=0\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(f(x)=x^2+2x-3\)
        \(g(x)=x+3\)
        
        \((\frac{f}{g})(x) =\) ___________
        
        \(f(-3) =\) ___________
     </para>
    <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  
  <para>\((\frac{f}{g})(x)=x-1\)
\(f(-3)=0\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<para>The Remainder Theorem states that if a polynomial function \(f(x)\) is divided by \(x-c\), then the remainder is \(f(c)\). This means we can always compare the remainder by finding \(f(c)\) when the divisor is written in the form \(x-c\).</para>

<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise id="_1354241e-b60c-45b8-951b-099be0a8eba8" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Use the Remainder Theorem to find the remainder when \(f(x)=x^3-7x+12\) is divided by \(x + 3\).</para>
        <para>Enter the remainder here.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The remainder is 6</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 6</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_53f4a375-e2b9-4945-a16f-9fc9e4fd3361" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the remainder here.</para><para>Use the Remainder Theorem to find the remainder when \(f(x)=2x^3-6x-24\) is divided by \(x - 3\).</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The remainder is 12</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 12</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
